# Monorepo PR Hygiene

Rules for creating clean, CI-passing commits in the Paperclip monorepo.

## Commit Discipline

### Never use `git add -A` or `git add .`

In a monorepo with multiple features in flight, broad staging commands sweep in
unrelated changes. Always stage files explicitly:

```bash
git add path/to/specific/file.ts
```

If you need to stage many files, build the list first and review it:

```bash
git diff --name-only | grep 'runtime-profile\|your-feature-keyword'
```

### One feature per commit

Each commit should touch files related to exactly one feature. If `git diff --name-only`
shows files across unrelated domains (e.g., routines + runtime profiles + company settings),
split them into separate commits or exclude the unrelated ones.

### Always diff against upstream before pushing

```bash
git diff --name-only origin/master..HEAD
```

Review every file. If you see something you didn't intentionally change, restore it:

```bash
git checkout origin/master -- path/to/unrelated/file
```

## Package.json Export Maps

Never commit local development export map changes. The repo uses `./src/*.ts` exports
for development and `./dist/*.js` for publishing. CI typechecks before building, so
`dist/` references will 404.

If you see this in a diff, restore the upstream version:

```bash
git checkout origin/master -- packages/*/package.json
```

## Barrel Export Files (index.ts)

When modifying `packages/shared/src/types/index.ts`, `packages/shared/src/index.ts`,
or `packages/shared/src/validators/index.ts`:

1. Only add exports for types/schemas that exist in files included in your PR
2. Never add re-exports for types from other features (company routines, mission control, etc.)
3. After editing, verify every `from "./module.js"` references a file that is either
   (a) unchanged from upstream or (b) included in your PR

## Lockfile Policy

Never commit `pnpm-lock.yaml`. The repo CI rejects PRs containing lockfile changes.
If it gets staged:

```bash
git reset HEAD pnpm-lock.yaml
git checkout -- pnpm-lock.yaml
```

## CI Workflow Syntax

- Use `cd server && pnpm vitest run ...` instead of `pnpm -C server vitest run ...`
- Place simulation/smoke scripts AFTER the `pnpm build` step (tsx needs compiled packages)
- Test workflow changes by checking step ordering in the YAML before pushing

## Pre-Push Validation

Run `./scripts/pre-push-check.sh` before every force-push to a PR branch. It catches
all 7 categories of CI failure automatically.

## Fork Workflow

When the authenticated user lacks push access to the upstream repo:

1. Fork via `gh repo fork <org>/<repo> --clone=false`
2. Add remote: `git remote add fork https://github.com/<user>/<repo>.git`
3. Push to fork: `git push -u fork <branch>`
4. Open cross-fork PR: `gh pr create --repo <org>/<repo> --head <user>:<branch>`
5. Rebase onto latest upstream before pushing: `git fetch origin master && git rebase origin/master`
